1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,007
From lesson observation to a plan for every teacher.

2
00:00:04,007 --> 00:00:08,840
Here is what the system does today, and where staff voice fits into it.

3
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:11,982
One form for every R3 lesson observation.

4
00:00:11,982 --> 00:00:23,518
June brought a hundred and sixty eight submissions, because inspectors observed in pairs; the system resolves those into a hundred and ten distinct lessons across a hundred and four teachers.

5
00:00:23,518 --> 00:00:25,825
Nothing typed twice, nothing counted twice.

6
00:00:26,275 --> 00:00:29,911
Those lessons land on one board: the round at a glance.

7
00:00:29,911 --> 00:00:30,903
How many lessons.

8
00:00:30,903 --> 00:00:31,894
How many teachers.

9
00:00:31,894 --> 00:00:34,539
Where judgements sit on the six point scale.

10
00:00:34,539 --> 00:00:37,183
What is working, and where to focus next.

11
00:00:37,633 --> 00:00:40,127
Every claim on that board carries a number.

12
00:00:40,127 --> 00:00:46,049
Open it for the lessons behind the claim, the inspector's own words, and a link to the locked record.

13
00:00:46,049 --> 00:00:48,543
Over six hundred references sit behind June alone.

14
00:00:48,543 --> 00:00:50,413
No statement stands on its own.

15
00:00:50,863 --> 00:00:52,284
From there, four steps.

16
00:00:52,284 --> 00:00:53,705
The observation is filed.

17
00:00:53,705 --> 00:00:55,126
The teacher gets feedback.

18
00:00:55,126 --> 00:01:00,454
The observer receives an analysis and a suggested coaching plan to approve, edit, or rewrite.

19
00:01:00,454 --> 00:01:06,137
And the teacher receives that plan, every suggestion referenced back to our own Student Progress Rubric.

20
00:01:06,587 --> 00:01:08,511
This is what the observer receives.

21
00:01:08,511 --> 00:01:12,360
This teacher is Acceptable on progress in lessons; the plan targets Good.

22
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:19,095
The rubric line for that level, one concrete move, what to look for next lesson, and where the technique comes from.

23
00:01:19,095 --> 00:01:21,661
The observer approves, edits, or writes their own.

24
00:01:22,111 --> 00:01:24,515
What the loop does not hear yet is the teacher.

25
00:01:24,515 --> 00:01:31,487
We capture how a session was rated, not what the teacher made of it, what they expect to struggle with, or what they will do differently on Monday morning.

26
00:01:31,936 --> 00:01:33,200
So, the first addition.

27
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,728
An evaluation of the professional learning session itself.

28
00:01:35,728 --> 00:01:42,996
Short, completed by the teacher, in place before the coaching plan is drafted, so the observer and the analysis both see it first.

29
00:01:43,446 --> 00:01:44,236
The second addition.

30
00:01:44,236 --> 00:01:46,342
A reflection and an action plan, six things.

31
00:01:46,342 --> 00:01:48,185
What the teacher took from the session.

32
00:01:48,185 --> 00:01:50,029
The challenges they expect in applying it.

33
00:01:50,029 --> 00:01:51,872
Their own ideas for getting past those.

34
00:01:51,872 --> 00:01:53,978
How they will use it in their classroom.

35
00:01:53,978 --> 00:01:55,821
What they need from their middle leader.

36
00:01:55,821 --> 00:01:58,981
And what they expect to change in student learning, over what timeframe.

37
00:01:59,431 --> 00:02:08,085
Each answer meets something ready made: five coaching strategies with worked examples, mapped point by point onto the Student Progress Rubric, built on our own Teaching and Learning Agenda.

38
00:02:08,085 --> 00:02:10,473
Observer and analysis draw from the same shelf.

39
00:02:10,473 --> 00:02:14,949
The teacher gets something recognisably ours, and the observer spends minutes rather than an evening.

40
00:02:15,399 --> 00:02:18,690
Staff responses then get the same treatment as the observation data.

41
00:02:18,690 --> 00:02:21,383
Themes across the school, not a folder of replies.

42
00:02:21,383 --> 00:02:22,879
Where support is asked for.

43
00:02:22,879 --> 00:02:24,375
Which challenges repeat, and where.

44
00:02:24,375 --> 00:02:27,666
All of it carrying references, exactly as the observation claims do.

45
00:02:28,116 --> 00:02:30,368
Middle leaders see their own team, and nobody else's.

46
00:02:30,368 --> 00:02:31,869
Not a report to read through.

47
00:02:31,869 --> 00:02:36,123
A starting point for a coaching conversation, with the teacher's own words already in front of them.

48
00:02:36,573 --> 00:02:43,997
Which gives every teacher what the observation already gives them: a plan of their own, built from their own lesson and their own words, in language the school already uses.

49
00:02:44,447 --> 00:02:47,306
The two forms are new; the architecture is not.

50
00:02:47,306 --> 00:02:52,707
Same intake, same evidence rules, same dashboard, same privacy layer, the data staying in our own database.

51
00:02:52,707 --> 00:02:55,249
Student surveys run on the same rails next.
